in this quaint midlothian neighborhood  giving back isn't unusual  but giving thanks in this special way is  something new  anthony the awesome ups our ups driver  anthony is the most kind and caring  deliberate person i've ever met anthony  gaskin drives this route through  halsley almost every day  she  in many ways he's become like family i  joked with him  back in june that i was going to add him  to my christmas card list because i  actually do see him more than family  he's you know always  stopping saying hi how are you how is  your mom how is your dad  it's just what many say they've needed  over the past  year the kindness that he spreads is  just unreal and especially during this  difficult time  to have anthony around is just it's  truly amazing this overall personality  demeanor  is so contagious that he was just like  what we needed in 2020. this sentiment  inspired patti friedman to send an email  to her neighbors  just in my own situation of kind of  feeling lonely and  trying to get my feet on the ground that  that he was bringing such  joy into my life together they came up  with a plan  to line the streets and thank the humble  man  who's made 2020 a little brighter  watching the video footage  i have watched it probably way too many  times i've sobbed  many tears just watching it because he  is such  an amazing person his smile is  infectious apparently anthony's story  has had a similar impact around the  world  on the cbs 6 page alone it's reached  more than 35 million people  it was meant to be it was going to  happen one way or the other not shocking  to anthony's own colleagues and friends  we all felt the same way  and the community he so graciously  serves i  didn't think he would be that emotional  but when i like it always teared me up a  little bit when i saw him i was like  yeah  you definitely deserve it in every way  well it shouldn't come as a surprise  that anthony was a little too busy for  an interview this time of year  in fact his friends say he hasn't even  read over the messages that are pouring  in  from around the world reporting in  chesterfield county tracy sears  cbs 6 news
 

